{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Terminal & Shell Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Know your shell"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Check which shell you're running:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "echo $SHELL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Most systems use `bash` or `zsh`. Both work fine. The commands in this course work in either."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Key things to know:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Move around"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cd ~/projects/ai-engineering-from-scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pwd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ls -la"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# History search (most useful shortcut you'll learn)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+R then type part of a previous command"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Press Ctrl+R again to cycle through matches"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Clear terminal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "clear   # or Ctrl+L"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Cancel a running command"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+C"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Suspend a running command (resume with fg)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+Z"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Piping and redirects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Piping connects commands together. This is how you process logs, filter output, and chain tools. You will use this constantly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Count how many times \"loss\" appears in a log"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cat train.log | grep \"loss\" | wc -l"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Extract just the loss values from training output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "grep \"loss:\" train.log | awk '{print $NF}' > losses.txt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Watch a log file update in real time, filtering for errors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tail -f train.log | grep --line-buffered \"ERROR\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Sort experiments by final accuracy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "grep \"final_accuracy\" results/*.log | sort -t= -k2 -n -r"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Redirect stdout and stderr to separate files"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python train.py > output.log 2> errors.log"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Redirect both to the same file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python train.py > train_full.log 2>&1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The three redirects you need:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Symbol | What it does |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|--------|-------------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `>` | Write stdout to file (overwrite) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `>>` | Append stdout to file |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `2>` | Write stderr to file |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `2>&1` | Send stderr to same place as stdout |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `\\|` | Send stdout of one command as stdin to the next |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Background processes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Training runs take hours. You don't want to keep your terminal open the whole time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Run in background (output still goes to terminal)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python train.py &"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Run in background, immune to hangup (closing terminal won't kill it)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nohup python train.py > train.log 2>&1 &"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Check what's running in background"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "jobs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ps aux | grep train.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Bring a background job to foreground"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "fg %1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Kill a background process"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "kill %1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# or find its PID and kill that"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "kill $(pgrep -f \"train.py\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The difference between `&`, `nohup`, and `screen`/`tmux`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Method | Survives terminal close? | Can reattach? |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|--------|-------------------------|---------------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `command &` | No | No |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `nohup command &` | Yes | No (check log file) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `screen` / `tmux` | Yes | Yes |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For anything longer than a few minutes, use tmux."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: tmux"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux lets you create persistent terminal sessions with multiple panes. This is the single most useful tool for managing training runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Install"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# macOS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "brew install tmux"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ubuntu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sudo apt install tmux"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Start a named session"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux new -s training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Split horizontally"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B then \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Split vertically"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B then %"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Navigate between panes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B then arrow keys"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Detach (session keeps running)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B then d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Reattach"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux attach -t training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# List sessions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux ls"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Kill a session"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux kill-session -t training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A typical AI workflow session:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tmux new -s train"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Pane 1: start training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python train.py --epochs 100 --lr 1e-4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B, \" to split, then run GPU monitor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "watch -n1 nvidia-smi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ctrl+B, % to split vertically, tail the logs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tail -f logs/experiment.log"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Now detach with Ctrl+B, d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# SSH out, go get coffee, come back"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# tmux attach -t train"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Monitoring with htop and nvtop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# System processes (better than top)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "htop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# GPU processes (if you have NVIDIA GPU)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Install: sudo apt install nvtop (Ubuntu) or brew install nvtop (macOS)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nvtop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Quick GPU check without nvtop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nvidia-smi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Watch GPU usage update every second"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "watch -n1 nvidia-smi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# See which processes are using the GPU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,name,used_memory --format=csv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`htop` keybindings you'll use:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `F6` or `>` to sort by column (sort by memory to find memory leaks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `F5` to toggle tree view (see child processes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `F9` to kill a process"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `/` to search for a process name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: SSH for remote GPU boxes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "When you rent a cloud GPU (Lambda, RunPod, Vast.ai), you connect via SSH."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Basic connection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ssh user@gpu-box-ip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# With a specific key"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ssh -i ~/.ssh/my_gpu_key user@gpu-box-ip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Copy files to remote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scp model.pt user@gpu-box-ip:~/models/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Copy files from remote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scp user@gpu-box-ip:~/results/metrics.json ./"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Sync a whole directory (faster for many files)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rsync -avz ./data/ user@gpu-box-ip:~/data/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Port forward (access remote Jupyter/TensorBoard locally)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ssh -L 8888:localhost:8888 user@gpu-box-ip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Now open localhost:8888 in your browser"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# SSH config for convenience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Add to ~/.ssh/config:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Host gpu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     HostName 192.168.1.100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     User ubuntu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/gpu_key"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Then just:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ssh gpu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Useful aliases for AI work"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add these to your `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "source phases/00-setup-and-tooling/10-terminal-and-shell/code/shell_aliases.sh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Or copy the ones you want. The key aliases:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# GPU status at a glance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alias gpu='nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,name,utilization.gpu,memory.used,memory.total,temperature.gpu --format=csv,noheader'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Kill all Python training processes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alias killtraining='pkill -f \"python.*train\"'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Quick virtual environment activate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alias ae='source .venv/bin/activate'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Watch training loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alias watchloss='tail -f logs/*.log | grep --line-buffered \"loss\"'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/shell_aliases.sh` for the full set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 8: Common AI terminal patterns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "These come up repeatedly in practice:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Run training, log everything, notify when done"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python train.py 2>&1 | tee train.log; echo \"DONE\" | mail -s \"Training complete\" you@email.com"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Compare two experiment logs side by side"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "diff <(grep \"accuracy\" exp1.log) <(grep \"accuracy\" exp2.log)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Find the largest model files (clean up disk space)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "find . -name \"*.pt\" -o -name \"*.safetensors\" | xargs du -h | sort -rh | head -20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Download a model from Hugging Face"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wget https://huggingface.co/model/resolve/main/model.safetensors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Untar a dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tar xzf dataset.tar.gz -C ./data/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
